From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:38:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): make the phone Settings menu read as a list of
 pages

On phones the Settings drawer is the whole menu, but it looked exactly
like the sidebar: bare /settings highlighted General although no page
was open, rows had no disclosure cue, and rows stayed about 33px tall
while the primary navigation already has 44px touch targets.

At phone widths the settings nav now shows a large Settings title, a
chevron Back row, sections as rounded inset groups with hairline
separators, and 44px rows with a trailing chevron. Bare /settings no
longer marks a row as current; once a page is open its row stays
marked. Desktop and tablet widths are unchanged.

Not upstream yet: proposed from feat/mobile-settings-nav; drop this copy once it merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Docs: none (layout polish of the phone Settings menu; nothing to configure)
(cherry picked from commit 03d8aec51f884c2ceb7c2907847641ceb78d8ab8)
